### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted by multiple lines of evidence. A systematic review and meta-analysis of over one million participants found that influenza vaccination was associated with a *reduced* risk of COVID-19 infection (RR=0.83) [source](https://pesquisa.bvsalud.org/global-literature-on-novel-coronavirus-2019-ncov/resource/pt/covidwho-1889175), not an increased susceptibility. Adjusted analyses accounting for confounders like age and comorbidities showed no link between flu vaccination and higher COVID-19 incidence or severity [source](https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/journal-of-clinical-and-translational-science/article/safety-of-influenza-vaccine-during-covid19/C26A417046677E65D421AD33B3E6281F). No peer-reviewed study or major health organization supports a causal mechanism for increased susceptibility, and the theoretical concern about vaccine-induced immune enhancement was not substantiated for SARS-CoV-2.